// PARAM: --analysis int
// y := x * 2 gives y an even/mod-2-congruent-to-0 fact from Times' own
// abstract transfer, for any x (x itself is left unconstrained). Two
// nested guards then bound y to the interval [1,2] via real control flow
// (0 < y, y < 3). Interval alone only knows y in {1,2} and cannot exclude
// 1; Congruence/Sign alone know nothing about the bound at all. The
// composite intersects [1,2] with "even" and gets the singleton {2}
// exactly -- verified that neither --analysis interval nor --analysis
// sign alone proves y == 2 on this identical source (both report
// UNKNOWN), matching 01-refinement_beats_components.vimp's contrast but
// driven by real multiplication instead of an equality guard, so the
// congruence fact comes from arithmetic (Int_Arithmetic.thy's Times case)
// rather than from a solved linear equation.
void main() {
  int32 x, y, z;
  y := x * 2;
  if (0 < y) {
    if (y < 3) {
      __voblint_check(y == 2) // PROVED
    } else {
      z := 0
    }
  } else {
    z := 0
  }
}
